--32 --no-assertions --datarace --unwind 2 --rounds 2 --no-por
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
B[0] = A[0] in one thread, B[M] = A[M] in another: with M == 0 they race
on B[0]. The race encoding gives each array access a location. Thread 1's store to
the split element B[[0]] got the default location, thread 3's got M, the index
of the read A[M] in the stored value, so the two never matched. Only the
event's own object gives a location now.
Reduced from weaver/popl20-more-parray-copy (no-data-race, expected false).
See race_location_other_array_safe (M >= 1), which must stay SUCCESSFUL.
